{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum product from pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    It iterates through the tuples, computes each product, and returns the smallest product found.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_prod = None\n\n    for a, b in tuple_list:\n        current_prod = a * b\n        if min_prod is None or current_prod < min_prod:\n            min_prod = current_prod\n            \n    return min_prod"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Union\n\nNumber = Union[int, float]\n\ndef _is_numeric(value: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is numeric (int or float) and not a boolean.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool)\n\ndef _to_numeric(value: Any) -> Number:\n    \"\"\"Returns the value as a numeric type, assuming it's already validated.\"\"\"\n    return value\n\ndef min_val(list_arg: List[Any]) -> Number:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value (int or float) in a heterogeneous list,\n    ignoring non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_values = [ _to_numeric(v) for v in list_arg if _is_numeric(v) ]\n    return min(numeric_values)"}
