{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a key-value dictionary using adjacent elements.\n    Validates input type and length, applying last-occurrence semantics for duplicate keys.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate_type(data):\n        if not isinstance(data, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"input must be a tuple\")\n\n    def validate_even_length(data):\n        if len(data) % 2 != 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"tuple must contain an even number of elements\")\n\n    def pair_adjacent_elements(data):\n        result_dict = {}\n        # Iterate over the tuple, taking two elements at a time for key and value.\n        for i in range(0, len(data), 2):\n            key = data[i]\n            value = data[i+1]\n            result_dict[key] = value\n        return result_dict\n\n    validate_type(input_tuple)\n    validate_even_length(input_tuple)\n    return pair_adjacent_elements(input_tuple)"}
