{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list, rotation_count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Handles empty lists and rotations greater than list length using modulo arithmetic.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective number of rotations\n    k = rotation_count % n\n\n    # If k is 0, no rotation is needed, return a copy of the original list\n    if k == 0:\n        return list(input_list) # Return a copy to match the design's \"input_list.copy()\"\n\n    # Otherwise, perform the rotation using slicing\n    return input_list[-k:] + input_list[:-k]"}
